To meet the City's requirements, we will deploy our solution on a SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, ensuring data sovereignty and compliance with EU regulations. Our solution will integrate with the City's existing information systems using APIs, ensuring seamless authentication and authorization. We will also implement measures to protect data, such as encryption and anonymization, and ensure that our solution respects the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR).

Our technical architecture will provide a response time below 2 seconds, with a p95 response time of 1800 ms, and an availability of 99.92%, exceeding the City's requirements. We will also ensure that our solution is designed as a tool of assistance, with no decision automated without explicit validation by an agent.

To address the City's environmental constraints, we will propose a solution that contributes to the reduction of energetic consumption. Our digital sobriety practices, such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and green IT hardware procurement policy, will reduce energy consumption by approximately 35%. We will also partner with green hosting providers, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, which use 100% renewable energy and have low Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) ratings.

Our solution will be designed to provide explanations for recommendations or proposals issued by the solution. We will employ explainability methods, such as source citation, chain-of-thought display, or SHAP for classification models, to ensure transparency and trust in our AI decision-making process.

We will conduct a pilot phase on a limited scope, followed by a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services. Our accompaniment to change and training actions will ensure that agents are equipped to use the new solution effectively.

Our pricing model targets a gross margin of 28%, but we also have a minimum acceptable margin of 18%. We estimate that our projected revenue for this contract over four years could be in line with our pricing model, assuming efficient resource allocation and cost optimization. Our cost-optimization strategies will include renegotiating rates with subcontractors if necessary, as indicated by our budget reduction impact analysis.

Our consortium has the necessary expertise and experience to deliver a high-quality solution that meets the City's requirements. We have led 8 consortia and have experience with partner management, which will ensure seamless integration with existing practices and continuity of processing files between agents and services. Our known partners, such as EuroCloud Solutions S.A., LexIA GmbH, and GreenCompute S.r.l., will contribute their expertise in sovereign cloud hosting, legal AI, and green IT to meet the regulatory and environmental constraints.

We are confident that our proposed solution will provide a coherent and comprehensive response to the City of Belval's call for tenders. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in more detail and demonstrate how our consortium can support the City's digital transformation strategy.
